well o 3 o; believe it or not, I did a lot of copy/pasting from the base sprites that where available in MV's files. All things that are bulls, cows, camels, goats, even the pig where largely resized/edited parts from the horse for example with lots of remaking or tweaking in between.
The software I use is actually a very old version of paintshop pro, version 7.04 specifically, and I don't necessarily recommend it as it's not particularly newbie friendly. Still it has a lot of perks, I like how it handles pixels, and since it's an older program it tends to render things out more pixelated then newer programs which is fantastic for sprite work and it does come with an animation shop so I can quickly make animation edits and test things from there. It can open up any photoshop file, and can run most photoshop plugins too. I've been using it since the days of RPG maker 2000~

